  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "What is the value of the ratio\n\n\\[\\dfrac{2^{2001} \\cdot 3^{2003}}{6^{2002}}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{6}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{2}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Use \\(6=2\\cdot3\\) to put the numerator and denominator in the same bases:\n\\[\n\\frac{2^{2001}\\cdot3^{2003}}{6^{2002}}\n=\\frac{2^{2001}\\cdot3^{2003}}{2^{2002}\\cdot3^{2002}}.\n\\]\nCancel the common, nonzero factors \\(2^{2001}\\) and \\(3^{2002}\\). One factor of \\(3\\) remains in the numerator, and one factor of \\(2\\) remains in the denominator. Thus the ratio is \\(\\frac32\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
